<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>SongLinkr — Harry Day</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="description"
        content="SongLinkr — an iOS app that converts music links between streaming platforms, built by Harry Day.">
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow">
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
    <meta name="language" content="English">
    <meta name="author" content="Harry Day">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#FF9400">
    <meta name="apple-itunes-app" content="app-id=1561986085">

    <!-- Favicon -->
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32x32.png">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16x16.png">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
    <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest">

    <!-- Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Harry Day">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:title" content="SongLinkr — Harry Day">
    <meta property="og:url" content="{{.SiteURL}}/songlinkr">
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{.SiteURL}}/images/songlinkr/socialimage.png">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="SongLinkr — get music links for any service">
    <meta property="og:description"
        content="SongLinkr — an iOS app that converts music links between streaming platforms, built by Harry Day.">

    <!-- Twitter -->
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    <meta name="twitter:site" content="@harrydayexe">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="SongLinkr — Harry Day">
    <meta name="twitter:description"
        content="SongLinkr — an iOS app that converts music links between streaming platforms, built by Harry Day.">
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{.SiteURL}}/images/songlinkr/socialimage.png">
    <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="SongLinkr — get music links for any service">

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/tailwind.css">
    {{if eq .Environment "local"}}
    <script>
        const es = new EventSource("/reload");
        es.onerror = () => {es.close(); setTimeout(() => location.reload(), 1500);};
    </script>
    {{end}}
</head>

<body class="bg-paper text-ink font-serif antialiased">
    {{template "header" .}}
    <main class="max-w-[640px] lg:max-w-[768px] mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-4">
        <div class="space-y-16">

            <header class="space-y-6">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
                    <img src="/images/songlinkr/AppIcon.svg" alt="SongLinkr app icon"
                        class="w-16 h-16 rounded-2xl shrink-0">
                    <div>
                        <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">SongLinkr</h1>
                        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted mt-1">Get music links for any
                            service</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xl leading-[1.55]">
                    An iOS app that converts music links between streaming platforms, so whatever you're sent, you
                    can open it wherever you actually listen. Built natively in Swift and SwiftUI, it's picked up
                    over 4,000 downloads through word of mouth alone.
                </p>
                <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/songlinkr/id1561986085" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="inline-block">
                    <img src="/images/songlinkr/AppStoreBadge/BlackBadge.svg" alt="Download on the App Store"
                        class="h-11 dark:hidden">
                    <img src="/images/songlinkr/AppStoreBadge/WhiteBadge.svg" alt="Download on the App Store"
                        class="h-11 hidden dark:block">
                </a>
                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-rule bg-paper-deep p-6 flex justify-center">
                    <img src="/images/songlinkr/HeroImageLight.png" alt="SongLinkr showing a converted song link"
                        class="max-w-[240px] w-full rounded-xl">
                </div>
            </header>

            <section class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-12">
                {{template "section-label" "Any song, any platform"}}
                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <p class="text-base leading-[1.65]">
                        The idea started with a familiar annoyance: sharing a song with a friend, only for them to
                        complain it's on the wrong streaming service. SongLinkr takes a link to a song or album
                        and gives you the freedom to open it on whichever platform you actually use.
                    </p>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-rule bg-paper-deep p-6 flex justify-center">
                        <img src="/images/songlinkr/LinkHeroImageLight.png"
                            alt="SongLinkr converting a link between platforms" class="max-w-[220px] w-full rounded-xl">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-12">
                {{template "section-label" "Results from across the web"}}
                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <p class="text-base leading-[1.65]">
                        Search results are powered by the <a href="https://song.link" target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="font-semibold hover:text-accent hover:border-b hover:border-accent transition-[color,border-color] duration-150">Song.Link</a>
                        API, covering a wide and growing range of platforms — Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube,
                        SoundCloud, Deezer, and many more.
                    </p>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-rule bg-paper-deep p-6 flex justify-center">
                        <img src="/images/songlinkr/ListFeatureImageLight.png"
                            alt="SongLinkr listing results across streaming platforms"
                            class="max-w-[220px] w-full rounded-xl">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-12">
                {{template "section-label" "Shazam, built in"}}
                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <p class="text-base leading-[1.65]">
                        Shazam's recognition technology is built into the app, so you can identify whatever's playing
                        around you — in a shop, a restaurant, or on the radio — and get it onto your platform of
                        choice. Matches sync back to your Shazam library too.
                    </p>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-rule bg-paper-deep p-6 flex justify-center">
                        <img src="/images/songlinkr/ShazamFeatureImageLight.png" alt="SongLinkr showing a Shazam match"
                            class="max-w-[220px] w-full rounded-xl">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-12">
                {{template "section-label" "A few more details"}}
                <ul class="space-y-4 text-base leading-[1.65]">
                    <li><span class="font-semibold">Clipboard-aware.</span> If you have a link copied when you open the
                        app, it's pasted in automatically.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-semibold">Set-and-forget defaults.</span> Choose a favourite platform once
                        and results open there automatically from then on.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-semibold">Share extension.</span> Send a link to SongLinkr directly from any
                        share sheet.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-semibold">Light and dark.</span> Follows the system appearance, day or
                        night.</li>
                    <li><span class="font-semibold">Translated.</span> Available in English, Spanish, and German.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="space-y-4">
                <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] mt-2 space-y-1.5">
                    <div class="text-muted">2021 &ndash; Present</div>
                    <div class="text-accent">Swift &middot; SwiftUI</div>
                </div>
                <p class="font-mono text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                    Powered by <a href="https://song.link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        class="hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-150">Song.Link</a>.
                    SongLinkr is not actively developed further, but remains available and supported.
                </p>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
                    <a href="/songlinkr/privacy"
                        class="text-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-150">Privacy Policy</a>
                    <a href="/songlinkr/support"
                        class="text-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-150">Support</a>
                </div>
                <p class="font-mono text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                    Apple, the Apple logo and iPhone are trademarks of Apple Inc., registered in the U.S. and other
                    countries. App Store is a service mark of Apple Inc.
                </p>
            </section>

        </div>
    </main>
    {{template "footer" .}}
</body>

</html>

{{define "section-label"}}
<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted shrink-0">{{.}}</h2>
    <hr class="flex-1 border-0 border-t border-rule m-0">
</div>
{{end}}
